cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Knap in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Knap: a pure Mojo byte level BPE tokenizer"
abstract: >-
  Knap is a byte level Byte Pair Encoding tokenizer written in pure Mojo.
  It implements the seven encodings that OpenAI's models use and runs with
  no Python interpreter in the process, so that a Mojo or MAX application
  can tokenize inside its own runtime. Correctness is treated as the
  product: every encoding is differentially tested against the reference
  implementation over a 110 MB corpus, every token id in every encoding is
  decoded and compared, and the benchmarks publish the cases where other
  implementations win. Its contribution is as much the method as the
  library, and the negative results are published alongside the positive
  ones.
type: software
